<description>&lt;p&gt;Prime Minister Al-Zaidi has taken direct control of Iraq's intelligence service while Iran has stepped up pressure on Baghdad over PJAK armed presence. Al-Zaidi's visit to Damascus revived the Sharaa pipeline dispute but also moved forward talks on border security and oil exports, prompting the parliamentary security committee to consider funding for enhanced air-defence systems. Iraqi security agencies arrested nine suspects on human-trafficking charges and a parliamentarian was sentenced for illegal oil contracts. The Kurdistan region deepened security coordination with Baghdad and advanced weapons-control measures. 396 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuwFBVV95cUxPcng4NWpfejc2anBFRkI0Z3NqX3piQzE5b1hMTWtFV1VWTDcwbkQ3QlFiR3VpSm9hS08zbWFIclNSeXNfemg1eFJYb3VPRVJ1dVRfVHYzdG1mekdHeTRkWmpNV2xiUFdDbXp5bml4TnFOS1RMM2NEcXRLdlFGY1VzSy1aSDQwc1JBVlRaSFJmZEV5WUw3eUFqOWFWQ1RwUlhtMDZlWG9wZndiU20yTXZ6Z1dvN0dNdnNybWFr?oc=5&quot;&gt;The National&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxQUHJDOHZvbktKQ1VWV2JNVXVIQXFRdWRzRmdNWDI2dzRSMTRtUWNVZ1Z0b1I4N3ZLQ2Mza1JNUF9OMHQwemdtS1Y4LXZXeUdXSEJVUmVvZy1fcjJMd2JtNXllVDFYWnp3UDRaVnJ0S0t3X0JRSk5qMnd4blVfMHBiS0Ribm1IRVplbi1hT0x4dHEtUXdLa0VfVm9OMEd3blctUE0xSFczbXVxdmgwaUlBSG1SUGNWaG13czZjT3E2NXREaGs?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kurdistan24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxQalIzVjJueXhFZlN1cnVRXy1kOGpDOWZZc0RSSGhMbnpoTDBkdlQwTFBLQ041QlhFS21vYkhKdnVOcTFpQm05bUxlTUxyaEU0TlFqYkZScWpxWWI1WkxvS1llZnBPWWt4Sl9NY0g4dWNSVkk4S1NWbWl4Tk9zMmNtWFN3YVlBdmY2SWdiRXJveGVtaGV4QkJoYXBBUUNuek9OcDZLdUt2bXdpbE81NDNza3FWeDMyZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Amwaj.media&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;وكالة الانباء العراقية (واع)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quo